  "paragraph": 20,
  "text": "That brings us to Pillar Three: memory and durable state across sessions. On multi-hour engineering tasks, single-window agents tend to fail in two predictable ways. Either they try to one-shot an entire feature until context runs out halfway through a broken refactor, or they declare victory prematurely after fixing the happy path and lose track of subtle edge cases across dozens of steps. A single ephemeral chat thread is simply too fragile to hold the entire state of a long-running software project.",
